{"id":"G3544","lemma":"νομικός","transliteration":"nomikos","sayIt":"nomikos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"adjective","gloss":"lawyer","meaning":"νομικός, -ή, -όν\n(νόμος), [in LXX: 4Ma.5:4 * ;]\n1. relating to law: μάχαι, Tit.3:9.\n2. learned in the law; as subst., ὁ ν. (EV, lawyer): Mat.22:35, Luk.10:25, Tit.3:13; pl., Luk.7:30 11:45-46, 52 14:3 (cf. MM, xvii).†\nSYN.: γραμματεύς, q.v (AS)","glosses":["experts in the law","expert in the law","about the law","lawyer"],"count":9,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-22","v":35,"renderings":{"bsb":"an expert in the law","kjv":"which was a lawyer"}},{"chapterId":"luk-7","v":30,"renderings":{"bsb":"experts in the law","kjv":"lawyers"}},{"chapterId":"luk-10","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"expert in the law","kjv":"lawyer"}},{"chapterId":"luk-11","v":45,"renderings":{"bsb":"experts in the law","kjv":"of the lawyers"}},{"chapterId":"luk-11","v":46,"renderings":{"bsb":"experts in the law","kjv":"ye lawyers"}},{"chapterId":"luk-11","v":52,"renderings":{"bsb":"experts in the law","kjv":"lawyers"}},{"chapterId":"luk-14","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"experts in the law","kjv":"the lawyers"}},{"chapterId":"tit-3","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"about the law","kjv":"the law"}},{"chapterId":"tit-3","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"lawyer","kjv":"the lawyer"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 22:35","note":"One of them, a lawyer, asked him a question, testing him.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 7:30","note":"But the Pharisees and the lawyers rejected the counsel of God, not being baptized by him themselves.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Titus 3:9","note":"but shun foolish questionings, genealogies, strife, and disputes about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}